Priority: 1
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-text-tool, fix-text-tool-click-entry

Goal:
Make text entry commit only under explicit user control instead of unpredictably finalizing while the user is still typing.

Context:
The current text tool can open a text editor correctly, but the user reports that it sometimes stops input and places the text on the canvas too early. That strongly suggests the current accept/blur/idle logic is too eager for a desktop drawing workflow. The requested behavior is explicit control: the text should stay editable until the user deliberately accepts it, with `Esc` proposed as the main confirmation key.

Expected changes:

- inspect the current text-editor lifecycle and identify what currently triggers early commit
- remove any time-based or overly eager blur-based auto-accept behavior if present
- make text editing remain active until an explicit user action accepts it
- support `Esc` as the requested key to finish and place the text
- make the acceptance/cancel behavior visible and consistent so the user knows how text mode exits

Acceptance criteria:

- After placing a text editor, pauses in typing do not commit the text.
- Pressing `Esc` finalizes the current text into a canvas text item.
- Text does not get placed unexpectedly just because focus or timing changes momentarily.
- Empty text sessions still fail closed without creating junk items.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Keep this task focused on stable text-entry control, not re-editing old text items.
- If the current behavior also needs a cancel path, define it explicitly instead of leaving blur semantics ambiguous.
